{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Azt1rrgYQC4gBfsSp8TQ1o","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-15-2100-precompute-mle-fold-layout\n2\t\n3\tMLE Rounds is the most anti-scaling STARK component: 166ms at APC 300 vs 118ms at APC 0 (0.71x ratio, worse at APC 300 despite 2.35x fewer cells). The `fold_mle_evals` function calls `fold_pingpong` twice per round (mat_evals + selectors), each rebuilding 4 descriptor arrays via `to_device()` and launching a separate kernel — totaling 112 `to_device()` calls and 28 kernel launches per segment across 14 rounds. Pre-computing all fold descriptors once and bulk-uploading before the MLE loop, plus fusing the two per-round fold calls into a single kernel launch, eliminates 104 CUDA API calls and halves fold launches. Expected savings: 5-15ms at APC 300. The fold descriptor overhead is known to be small (~0.3-0.5μs per CUDA API call from prior measurement), so this is a modest improvement that primarily reduces noise in the MLE overhead budget.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"719c141a-1a84-4f89-a64a-f54435a4c1b4","uuid":"fad68a15-1b63-47dc-a53d-aaf139a66481","timestamp":"2026-04-15T19:41:03.684Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-15-2100-precompute-mle-fold-layout\n\nMLE Rounds is the most anti-scaling STARK component: 166ms at APC 300 vs 118ms at APC 0 (0.71x ratio, worse at APC 300 despite 2.35x fewer cells). The `fold_mle_evals` function calls `fold_pingpong` twice per round (mat_evals + selectors), each rebuilding 4 descriptor arrays via `to_device()` and launching a separate kernel — totaling 112 `to_device()` calls and 28 kernel launches per segment across 14 rounds. Pre-computing all fold descriptors once and bulk-uploading before the MLE loop, plus fusing the two per-round fold calls into a single kernel launch, eliminates 104 CUDA API calls and halves fold launches. Expected savings: 5-15ms at APC 300. The fold descriptor overhead is known to be small (~0.3-0.5μs per CUDA API call from prior measurement), so this is a modest improvement that primarily reduces noise in the MLE overhead budget.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
