es trace values by corresponding μ powers\n  - Accumulates result into FpExt (4x extension field)\n- **Note (line 38):** Depending on column count, should use shared memory to reduce the sum (optimization opportunity)\n\n**Launch Parameters (line 235):**\n```cuda\nauto [grid, block] = kernel_launch_params(stacked_height);\n```\n\n### 3. Relationship Between WHIR and Merkle Tree Operations\n\n**Files Involved:**\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/whir.rs` (GPU WHIR prover)\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` (Stacking/Merkle operations)\n\n**Merkle Tree Integration (WHIR lines 318-326):**\n- After sumcheck completion, Merkle tree is created for codewords\n- Line 318: `MerkleTreeGpu::<F, HS::Digest>::new_with_hash()` - constructs tree with hash\n- Line 320: Tree height = 1 << k_whir (folding factor determines tree structure)\n- Query proof generation happens at lines 399-404 for initial round, 445-464 for subsequent rounds\n\n**Stacked Reduction Integration:**\n- Stacking layout defined in `stacked_reduction.rs` with parameters `l_skip` and `n_stack`\n- Stacked height = 2^(l_skip + n_stack)\n- WHIR operates on stacked matrix with layout tracking (line 106-118)\n\n### 4. WHIR Scaling with AIR Count and Cells\n\n**Scaling Parameters (from `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/stark-backend/src/config.rs`):**\n\n- **SystemParams** (lines 54-67):\n  - `l_skip`: Skip domain bits (typically 2-4)\n  - `n_stack`: Number of stacking layers (varies by AIR count)\n  - `w_stack`: Max stacked matrix width = w_stack * 2^(n_stack + l_skip)\n  - `log_blowup`: Reed-Solomon rate parameter\n  - `k_whir`: Folding factor per round (default = 4, line 9)\n  - `log_final_poly_len`: Final polynomial size\n\n**Cell Count Calculation:**\n- Total cells = w_stack * 2^(n_stack + l_skip)\n- Affects num_packets in batching kernel (line 97 in whir.rs)\n- Each AIR contributes traces that get stacked and batched\n\n**Num WHIR Rounds Calculation (lines 286-288):**\n```rust\nlet num_rounds = log_stacked_height\n    .saturating_sub(whir_params.log_final_poly_len)\n    .div_ceil(k_whir);\n```\n- Formula: num_rounds = (log(stacked_height) - log_final_poly_len) / k_whir\n- More AIRs → larger n_stack → more WHIR rounds\n\n**Query Count Per Round (lines 297-301):**\n- Determined by proximity regime and target security bits\n- Unique decoding: max_agreement = (1 + ρ) / 2\n- num_queries = ceil(security_bits / per_query_bits)\n\n### 5. NTT/Bit-Reversal Operations in WHIR\n\n**Bit-Reversal in Batch NTT (file: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/batch_ntt_small.cu`):**\n\n- **Line 101-104:** Natural-to-bitreverse transform with template dispatch\n- **Line 108:** `rev_len()` computes bit-reversed index\n- **Lines 116-118:** Thread layout: threads_x = 2^l_skip, threads_y = 1024/2^l_skip\n- **Shared Memory (line 119):** Only if l_skip > LOG_WARP_SIZE (5), else registers + warp shuffle\n\n**MLE Interpolation (NTT-like operations):**\n- File: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/mle_interpolate.cu`\n- **Lines 159-166 in whir.rs:** Loop calling `mle_interpolate_stage_ext()` l_skip times\n- **Step sizes:** 1, 2, 4, ..., 2^(l_skip-1)\n- **Operation:** For each stage: buffer[i + step] -= buffer[i] (eval-to-coeff direction)\n\n**Fused MLE Interpolation (lines 141-163 in mle_interpolate.rs):**\n- `mle_interpolate_fused_2d()`: Fuses multiple stages using warp shuffle\n- Processes steps from start_step up to start_step << (num_stages-1)\n- Max 5 stages (warp shuffle constraint: step ≤ 16)\n\n### 6. `mle_interpolate_fused_2d_kernel` (Performance-Related)\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/mle_interpolate.cu` (lines 68-123)\n\n**Template Parameters:**\n- `EvalToCoeff`: Direction (true for eval→coeff, false for coeff→eval)\n- `NumStages`: Number of fused stages (1-5)\n- `BitReversed`: Access pattern (strided if true, contiguous if false)\n\n**Algorithm (lines 68-122