{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01F6J9Vtd29wwihhs9dSpHxG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments` function uses `as_ptr()` and `as_mut_ptr()` on the DeviceBuffers, and passes `height` as the logical size. The debug_asserts check `len() >= height/2` for the output buffers. So the function already supports oversized buffers (capacity > logical length) — it just needs `len() >= height/2`.\n\nThis means pre-allocated buffers with capacity >= max_height will work, as long as their `len()` is >= the required output_height at each round.\n\n\nSince `with_capacity` sets both `len` and `capacity` to the same value, a pre-allocated buffer with capacity = max_height will have `len = max_height`, which satisfies the debug_assert for any height/2. The kernel itself only reads and writes based on the `height` parameter, so it naturally ignores any extra capacity. The solution is to pre-allocate four buffers at maximum size and reuse them as ping-pong pairs across rounds.\n\nNow I need to verify that `whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round` also respects the height parameter in the same way.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":568,"cache_read_input_tokens":190876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":568},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"719c141a-1a84-4f89-a64a-f54435a4c1b4","uuid":"031e21dc-e93c-425c-be4b-b11cb8debc58"}
