{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0192j2U9RBSqVoCnLpNKoaKY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Pre-allocate WHIR Fold Buffers\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate per-round GPU memory allocation churn in the WHIR opening proof by pre-allocating `f_coeffs` and `w_moments` buffer pairs at maximum size and reusing them via a pingpong pattern across all inner sumcheck rounds. This targets the 125ms WHIR phase at APC 300 (regressed from 100ms baseline) by removing VPMM page creation/mapping overhead and stabilizing the GPU memory pool state for subsequent bandwidth-bound phases.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/whir.rs`, function `prove_whir_opening_gpu` (line 62)\n10\t\n11\tThe WHIR inner sumcheck loop (lines 202-271) runs `k_whir × num_whir_rounds` iterations (4 × 3 = 12 at APC 300, m=24, log_final_poly_len=12). Each iteration:\n12\t\n13\t1. **Line 218:** `let mut new_f_coeffs = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height);` — allocates fresh buffer\n14\t2. **Line 219:** `let mut new_w_moments = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(output_height);` — allocates fresh buffer\n15\t3. **Line 224:** `whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round(&f_coeffs, &w_moments, ...)` — reads from current buffers\n16\t4. **Line 255:** `whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments(&f_coeffs, &w_moments, &mut new_f_coeffs, &mut new_w_moments, ...)` — reads from current, writes to new\n17\t5. **Line 269-270:** `f_coeffs = new_f_coeffs; w_moments = new_w_moments;` — drops old buffers, replaces with new\n18\t\n19\t**Why it's slow:** For the first ~5 inner rounds at APC 300, buffer sizes are 128 MiB, 64 MiB, 32 MiB, 16 MiB, and 16 MiB. These exceed the 16 MiB VPMM page size threshold, so each allocation goes through VPMM (`cuMemCreate` + `cuMemMap` + `cuMemSetAccess`). Each deallocation does `cuMemUnmap` + `cuMemRelease`. The first round alone requires 16 new pages per buffer (128 MiB / 16 MiB page size), costing ~6.4ms per buffer (16 × 0.4ms per `cuMemCreate`). Subsequent rounds reuse freed pages but still pay mapping overhead (~50-100μs per operation). Total: ~12ms allocation overhead + ~12ms free overhead = ~24ms. Additionally, the repeated alloc/free pattern disturbs the VPMM pool's free region layout, degrading memory access patterns for bandwidth-bound kernels in subsequent phases — the same pool state sensitivity documented in `cache-codeword-buffer-across-segments`, `multistream-stacked-reduction-round0`, and `decouple-vpmm-pool-threshold` reports.\n20\t\n21\t**Key property enabling the optimization:** Both `whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round` and `whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments` use the explicit `height` parameter (not buffer `.len()`) to determine how many elements to read/write (verified at `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/whir.rs` lines 85-104, 118-131). The debug_asserts only require `len >= height` for inputs and `len >= height/2` for outputs. Pre-allocated buffers with capacity >= max height satisfy all assertions.\n22\t\n23\t## Changes\n24\t\n25\t### Change 1: Pre-allocate pingpong buffer pairs before the WHIR round loop\n26\t\n27\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/whir.rs`\n28\t\n29\t**What:** Before the outer `for (whir_round, ...)` loop (line 199), allocate two pairs of buffers at the maximum size needed (the initial `height`):\n30\t\n31\t```rust\n32\t// Pre-allocate pingpong buffers for sumcheck fold.\n33\t// Max size is the initial height; each round uses progressively less.\n34\tlet initial_height = 1 << m;\n35\tlet mut buf_a_f = f_coeffs;         // reuse the already-allocated f_coeffs as buf_a\n36\tlet mut buf_a_w = w_moments;         // reuse the already-allocated w_moments as buf_a\n37\tlet mut buf_b_f = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(initial_height);\n38\tlet mut buf_b_w = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(initial_height);\n39\t// Track which pair is \"current\" (input) vs \"next\" (output)\n40\tlet mut use_a_as_input = true;\n41\t```\n42\t\n43\t**Why:** Only 2 additional buffers are allocated (buf_b_f, buf_b_w) vs the current 24 allocations across 12 rounds. The initial `f_coeffs` and `w_moments` (already allocated at lines 148, 175) serve as buf_a. Total additional memory: `2 × initial_height × sizeof(EF) = 2 × 2^24 × 16 = 512 MiB`. At APC 300, peak GPU memory usage is ~15 GiB of 24 GiB — the 512 MiB increase is within budget.\n44\t\n45\t### Change 2: Replace per-round allocation with pingpong swap in the inner loop\n46\t\n47\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/whir.rs`\n48\t\n49\t**What:** Replace lines 218-270 (the allocation + fold + swap) with:\n50\t\n51\t```rust\n52\tlet (cur_f, cur_w, next_f, next_w) = if use_a_as_input {\n53\t    (&buf_a_f, &buf_a_w, &mut buf_b_f, &mut buf_b_w)\n54\t} else {\n55\t    (&buf_b_f, &buf_b_w, &mut buf_a_f, &mut buf_a_w)\n56\t};\n57\t\n58\t// sumcheck round reads from cur_f, cur_w\n59\tunsafe {\n60\t    whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round(cur_f, cur_w, &mut d_s_evals, &mut d_sumcheck_tmp, f_height as u32)?;\n61\t}\n62\t// ... transcript observe/sample (unchanged) ...\n63\t\n64\t// fold writes to next_f, next_w\n65\tunsafe {\n66\t    whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments(cur_f, cur_w, next_f, next_w, alpha, f_height as u32)?;\n67\t}\n68\tuse_a_as_input = !use_a_as_input;\n69\t```\n70\t\n71\t**Why:** No allocation or deallocation occurs within the inner loop. The `height` parameter tells kernels how much of the buffer to use.\n72\t\n73\t### Change 3: Extract the final f_coeffs after the inner loop for g_coeffs computation\n74\t\n75\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/whir.rs`\n76\t\n77\t**What:** After the inner loop (line 271), the \"current\" buffer (the one that was last written to) holds the folded result. Assign it back to a local reference for the g_coeffs computation (lines 272-354):\n78\t\n79\t```rust\n80\tlet f_coeffs_ref = if use_a_as_input { &buf_a_f } else { &buf_b_f };\n81\tlet _w_moments_ref = if use_a_as_input { &buf_a_w } else { &buf_b_w };\n82\t```\n83\t\n84\tUse `f_coeffs_ref` wherever `f_coeffs` was used for g_coeffs splitting (line 274+). The w_moments buffer is used later for `w_moments_accumulate` (line 501) — it needs a mutable reference, so use `buf_a_w` or `buf_b_w` directly based on `use_a_as_input`.\n85\t\n86\t**Why:** Avoids copying or transferring ownership. The pre-allocated buffers persist across WHIR rounds.\n87\t\n88\t### Change 4: Handle the d_sumcheck_tmp buffer\n89\t\n90\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/whir.rs`\n91\t\n92\t**What:** The `d_sumcheck_tmp` buffer (line 195) already uses a reuse-if-large-enough pattern (lines 215-216). Keep this unchanged — it's already optimal.\n93\t\n94\t## Invariants\n95\t\n96\t1. **Correctness:** The CUDA kernels (`whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round`, `whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments`) use the `height` parameter for all indexing. Pre-allocated oversized buffers produce identical results. The debug_asserts `len >= height` and `len >= height/2` are satisfied because `initial_height >= f_height >= output_height` for all rounds.\n97\t\n98\t2. **Memory safety:** Both buffer pairs are allocated before the loop and live until `prove_whir_opening_gpu` returns. No dangling pointers. The pingpong swap only changes which pair is read vs written — no ownership transfer.\n99\t\n100\t3. **Transcript consistency:** The sumcheck polynomial values (`d_s_evals`) and all transcript operations are unchanged. The optimization only changes allocation patterns, not computation.\n101\t\n102\t4. **APC 0 behavior:** At APC 0, the WHIR buffers are also large (height=2^24 for the 5 segments). The pre-allocation eliminates the same VPMM churn. No regression path since the buffers were going to be allocated anyway — they're just allocated upfront instead of per-round.\n103\t\n104\t## Measurement Plan\n105\t\n106\t1. Run `run_pairing.sh` for APC {0, 100, 300} and capture metrics.json.\n107\t2. Compare WHIR time using `spec.py`:\n108\t   - Primary: WHIR at APC 300 should decrease from 125ms (target: ≤110ms, matching or improving baseline 100ms)\n109\t   - Secondary: STARK excl trace at APC 300 should decrease\n110\t   - Regression check: APC 0 STARK excl trace must not increase by >20ms\n111\t3. Run nsight profiling at APC 300 and compare:\n112\t   - VPMM-related API calls (`cuMemCreate`, `cuMemMap`) count should decrease\n113\t   - No new GPU kernel time regression in LogUp GKR or other bandwidth-bound phases\n114\t\n115\t## Rollback Criteria\n116\t\n117\t- WHIR at APC 300 does not improve by at least 10ms (below noise threshold)\n118\t- STARK excl trace at APC 300 does not improve or regresses\n119\t- APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by more than 20ms\n120\t- Proof verification fails at any APC configuration\n121\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01B2aXHfTFY1CYrURnDvPBve","session_id":"719c141a-1a84-4f89-a64a-f54435a4c1b4","uuid":"f9e66fab-9b53-47d8-ae54-3da7db350990","timestamp":"2026-04-15T20:12:48.304Z"}
