{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TFvNMoAvA9fkXEfQMtCHjC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to continue from where I left off. I was updating the plan after the reviewer's feedback. Let me:\n\n1. Update the plan to address the correctness blocker and other findings\n2. Resubmit for review\n3. Finalize\n\nLet me re-read where I was. I had:\n- Read the `w_moments_accumulate` function and confirmed it uses `.len()` (line 148)\n- Identified the fix: scope pingpong to inner rounds 0..k_whir-2, last round allocates correctly-sized buffers\n\n\n- Verified the issue more carefully: the function reads `w_moments.len()` and passes it as height to the CUDA kernel, which would process too many elements with oversized buffers\n- The solution is to use pre-allocated pingpong buffers only for the first k_whir-1 inner rounds, then allocate correctly-sized output buffers for the final inner round of each WHIR outer round\n\nNow I'm updating the plan.md file to document these findings and resubmitting for review.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":204621,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":204621},"output_tokens":39,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"719c141a-1a84-4f89-a64a-f54435a4c1b4","uuid":"1539142d-5f68-4ea6-ae1b-401b541a58b3"}
