{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0144foAxt25uK7HfTYLpWGUU","type":"tool_result","content":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-15-2230-prealloc-whir-fold-buffers\n\nPre-allocate and reuse WHIR sumcheck fold buffers (`f_coeffs`, `w_moments`) via a pingpong pattern instead of allocating new DeviceBuffers each inner round. Currently, each of the k_whir × num_whir_rounds inner sumcheck rounds allocates two fresh DeviceBuffers (one for folded `f_coeffs`, one for folded `w_moments`) and frees the previous pair. For the first ~5 rounds at APC 300 (buffer sizes 128-16 MiB), these go through VPMM, creating page churn that disturbs GPU memory pool state for subsequent bandwidth-bound phases. The WHIR phase regressed 25ms from baseline (100ms → 125ms) coinciding with VPMM page size changes, suggesting pool state sensitivity. Pre-allocating at maximum size and alternating between two buffer pairs eliminates all per-round VPMM allocations/frees and stabilizes pool state.\n\n=== plan.md exists ===\n162 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-15-2230-prealloc-whir-fold-buffers/plan.md\n\n=== baseline exists ===\napc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\nnsys_apc300.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc300.sqlite\nsummary.md\n\n=== current metrics ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc000.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc100.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300_metrics.json\n\n=== nsight profile ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_nsys_apc300.nsys-rep\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_nsys_apc300.sqlite","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"719c141a-1a84-4f89-a64a-f54435a4c1b4","uuid":"90f0d720-fabc-47b7-9b13-b81d29a8dace","timestamp":"2026-04-15T22:04:51.590Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-15-2230-prealloc-whir-fold-buffers\n\nPre-allocate and reuse WHIR sumcheck fold buffers (`f_coeffs`, `w_moments`) via a pingpong pattern instead of allocating new DeviceBuffers each inner round. Currently, each of the k_whir × num_whir_rounds inner sumcheck rounds allocates two fresh DeviceBuffers (one for folded `f_coeffs`, one for folded `w_moments`) and frees the previous pair. For the first ~5 rounds at APC 300 (buffer sizes 128-16 MiB), these go through VPMM, creating page churn that disturbs GPU memory pool state for subsequent bandwidth-bound phases. The WHIR phase regressed 25ms from baseline (100ms → 125ms) coinciding with VPMM page size changes, suggesting pool state sensitivity. Pre-allocating at maximum size and alternating between two buffer pairs eliminates all per-round VPMM allocations/frees and stabilizes pool state.\n\n=== plan.md exists ===\n162 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-15-2230-prealloc-whir-fold-buffers/plan.md\n\n=== baseline exists ===\napc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\nnsys_apc300.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc300.sqlite\nsummary.md\n\n=== current metrics ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc000.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc100.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300_metrics.json\n\n=== nsight profile ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_nsys_apc300.nsys-rep\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_nsys_apc300.sqlite","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
